    "runtimeMinutes": 130,
    "watchedDate": "2024-01-03",
    "loggedDate": "2024-01-03",
    "rating": 4.0,
    "isRewatch": false,
    "isLiked": true,
    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "BROOOOO THE ENDING! \n\nicl when i was first watching it i was kinda uninterested in the film, it looked beautiful but there wasn’t anything in it that was really grasping my attention. but when ransom enters the story and marta’s story begins to properly unravel, it got REALLY good. and good LORD the reveal by blanc. at the end was genuinely insane, had my full complete focus the whole way through. and the film is SO SO SO rewarding because it doesn’t spoon feed you ANYTHING, that feeling when chris evan’s was about to stab ana de armas (gorgeous woman btw) and at the LAST moment i remembered that one dialogue that harlan said about not telling the difference between a real knife and a prop knife, and then THEY FUCKING REVEALED THAT HE STABBED HER WITH A PROP KNIFE 🤯. that sentence was written horribly but that was one of THE most rewarding feelings ive felt watching a movie in a long time. it really makes you feel bare smart and now im very excited to watch glass onion. apparently madelyn cline’s in it too (gorgeous woman btw) so im excited for that too. up until that sort of reveal scene about ransom the absolute highlights for me were the stunning cinematography and the BEAUTIFUL score. i was looking for a good movie to watch for my birthday and this one was definitely a great choice. fantastic way to start my 19th. W movie",
