    "review": "i didn’t expect to like this movie as much as i did ibr. i’ve been listening to bare hindi songs lately n kabira is lowkey one of my favourite songs EVER, n everyone said it was a good movie too so i thought id check it out . \n\nive only cried 3 times cos of a movie before and i DID NOT think this was gonna be the next 😭😭😭 but man every single scene after the second time they play kabira is jus death and torture.  deepika looked so good in the movie but that look w the hairband n glasses ☠️ oh my God thats horror. ranbir was a really really good actor too , ESPECIALLY in the more emotional scenes in the closing 45 mins of the film. \n\nbut arguably the best part of the movie was that MUSIC. i already knew it would be a banger cos of kabira but the score too was fantastic, it made the already emotional scenes EVEN harder to get through without crying. my favourites are kabira (obviously lol) kabira encore, ilahi and subanallah. \n\ni think it did get kind of boring like 1.5 or so hours in, it was when bunny n naina did the dance together for the bride’s side at that party. that whole sequence felt kinda dry to me , n i think if they cut it out it would elevate the movie by a lot more. cos lowkey by the final 30 mins i was like wow this is making me bare emotional but i was also like this is long asf. anyways purely cos of the ending the movie moved up by like 2 ratings it was actually so good. my review was only supposed to be like a line or two initially but it all changed cos the ending\n\nnext up is either rockstar (kun faya kun is my absolute favourite hindi song) or maybe rocky aur rani apparently it’s really good.",
