    "review": "i watched this movie months ago but never got round to making a review \n\nthis is a HUGELY emotional and powerful film, regardless of who’s watching the movie. siddharth’s performance was absolutely PHENOMENAL , bro there’s this one scene near the middle of the movie where he’s faking a smile whilst trying not to cry GOD this film is so amazing. also the child actors both were great, i can’t imagine how traumatising a film like this even is to act. \n\nbut anyway the part that acc made me deep my own life was one of the final scenes where nimisha’s character talks about her uncle i think it was and siddharths first instinct is to harm him for ‘revenge’, because that is genuinely exactly what i was thinking too. it made me realise a glaring flaw ab my personality in that i thought about causing harm to the perpetrator rather than looking after the victim. like that scene genuinely has changed the way i act since watching the movie and there are hardly ANY movies, lowkey none at all that have had that sort of effect on me. \n\nsanthosh narayanan as ALWAYS made the most banger soundtrack of all time, i mean unakku thaan bro COME ON how do you even compose something like that. i love him. \n\ni’m really really excited for chiyaan 62 now, the little announcement thing they made was already incredible , so i have high hopes for the film too.",
