    "review": "SPOILERS HALFWAY THROUGH!\ndamn man , i did NOT expect this movie to be this good or to be this emotional. add this to the list of films that almost made me cry. sohaib watched la la land (my fav film) so i asked him what his fav movie was n he said this and parasite , so i figured id watch it \n\nit’s 5.40am rn so im bare tried but man this film was genuinely amazing. everything from the end of the le mans race to the credits was just peak cinema. i don’t even know where to start the review but it might be a long one\n\nspeaking more generally the cinematography was fantastic , i managed to find a beautiful 4k hdr print so i didn’t have to use the netflix one n im glad i did, because the colours in this film are so gorgeous. damon’s blue shirt is such a nice colour lmao i want a top that colour. but anyway the cinematography not just during the races but just the scenery in general is beautiful, my favourite scenes were the night time scenes where he test drives the gt40 (i think it was anyway) for the first time outside shelby international. the cars headlights n heating brakes against the city lights in an otherwise dark blue frame looked SO gorgeous, i had to pause the movie there n take a screenshot. during the races too everything looked amazing, i might be tweaking but there were a couple spots where it did look a little video gamey but they’re so minor you can basically ignore it. \n\nthe audio too was fantastic , that 7 litre sounded MEAN . but obviously besides that the sound design in general was great , you can really feel the power of all these cars and it never feels like it’s being exaggerated for the movie or overwhelming , everything is really well balanced out. \n\nfor the performances i mean they were GREAT, obviously the star of the show bale was so so good, it felt weird hearing him w a brum accent and sounding more like real life him rather than the american accent i alwuas hear him in. there were these scenes where he’d kinda go into a flow state, for example the scenes when he’s at 7000+ rpm , the audio kinda drowns out and everything slows down (which is the last thing you’d expect) and it feels like we’re just moving through space, which is EXACTLY what damon’s monologue near the beginning says and i found it INCREDIBLE how they managed to bring that monologue to screen like that. bale’s character in general was really well played , you can really picture him as Miles and you can tell he feels like he’s at one with the car . theres this one which i talk ab in the spoiler part, which imo is the greatest acted scene in the whole movie, and is one of those moments where u take a moment to be like “this is great acting” .  idk if bale has any irl interest in cars but i wouldn’t be surprised if he did cos the way he talks about them and behaves whilst driving felt SO genuine. \n\nthe guy who played leo beebe kinda looks like jonah hill but maybe im tripping but anyway he was greatly done too you just can’t help but despise him. damon was fantastic also , ESPECIALLY in the final scene man he REALLY pulled thru in that scene when he was needed most. \n\nSPOILERS FROM NOW ON !!! but if you don’t plan on watching the movie read pls this part of the movie means quite a bit to me lol \n\nthe closing 30/40 minutes of the film was when the movie moved up from at 7.5 or so to a 8.5/9 for me, it REALLY elevated the film . when the race gets announced as a tie on that dumb technicality (i was really expecting it to be reversed somehow btw) you can’t help but feel insanely disappointed for miles, and the facial expressions that bale puts on during that critical scene only made it so much better. “you offered me the drive, not the win” man FUCK that line got me that’s when it started to get a lump in my throat. i felt so sorry for him at that moment especially when him n damon walked off into the sunset and the entire time he has this expression that on one hand shows that he is very upset but on the other shows that he’s insanely grateful for what he DID do. the scene building up to that moment was very well done too, again they had that flow state kinda scene where he was appreciating where he was at and considering henry ford’s proposal  , i genuinely couldn’t tell whether he’d slow down or not. that was one of my most memorable scenes imo. that whole sequence was masterfully done, loved every bit of it. \n\ni went into this film completely blind not even knowing what le mans was, i thought they actually drove for 24 hours straight 😭. so i didn’t know that ken miles was going to die, so that scene in the track where he does die was a REAL shock to me. but at the same time i loved how NOT dramatised it was. i especially loved damon in that scene, where he realised that miles won’t be able to get out of the car in time. i loved the build up they did an hour or so before the first time that miles got brake face and they explained how you can survive your car blowing up like that, cos it made the pay off SO much better. at first i was like they’ll just get him out but realising how far away miles was, seeing shelby give up, it dawns on you that yes, he is going to die. that scene also was incredibly done and i loved the way they made it a huge surprise when it happened. i’m happy he died doing what he loved 💔. but that scene again had me so close to tears man. seeing the smoke build up n then that glimpse of fire, seeing everyone but damon run towards him. everything after this is when damon really shines and you can absolutely tell how much miles means to him. yeah man his death scene and everything that comes after was very very very well done. \n\nit’s 6.10 now i can’t believe i spent half an hour writing this bro wtf 😭",
