    "review": "genuinely watched this movie like over a month ago but i really wanted to write another massive review for it cos i acc rly liked it but i kept delaying it 😭😭 n here i am writing it at 5.30 am HALF ASLEEP FAM\n\nanyway the movie was REALLY well made in every aspect except long legs himself ☠️. the cinematography was arguably the biggest strength of the film by a mile and there’s so many very cleverly crafted shots that RLY hooked me in\n\nmy favourite scenes r when the detectives in her study and instead of making her fill the frame , she’s off to the side and the rest of the shot is covered in darkness besides this doorway on the opposite side of the shot. EVERY time we were at that location i could NOT stop staring at the doorway instead of the lead (forgot her name its been a while) and i LOVED the way they did that so much. all the wide shots from inside the car were really nice too , the whole movie is just really pretty it reminded me of the batman in a way \n\nlong legs himself tho??  idk. when u imagine urself ACTUALLY being there with a donny like that i think id shit myself 300 times but seeing him on screen it was incredibly hard to picture him as this violent killer. especially when he did that stupid peek a boo dancer and that FUCKIMG “DaAAAaaAAaDDyYyYy” karaoke shit in his car BRO WHY DID THEY ADD THAT IN 😭. pissed me off so much when they released thag promo showing the actors heart beat seeing long legs for the first time, guys not even that scary hes jus ugly as FUCK and has a KNACKS voice bro FUCK LONGLEGS WTF 😭😭😭. ok i acc rly liked the movie idk why im hating. also the stupid fucking ending 20 mins felt so rushed and lazy cos it was like they just HAD to slap in a twist there somewhere to try end the film on a good note. the whole explanation behind why everything was happening in general felt like a bit of a cop out but that might just be cos of my personal beliefs meaning that the things in the film don’t really mean much to me. (idk how to say that without spoiling) \n\ni think this is a great example of hype killing art. the marketing team for this movie did absolutely insane , the promo was so so good and even tho i wasn’t able to interact w some of the phone number promos , all the teasers and poster were phenomenal and had a very different approach to it, which made me very excited. \n\nim too tired to write anymore and too silly to remember anything else ab the movie so night night",
