    "review": "💔 \n\n96 spoilers \n\nevery sign was pointing towards this film being an absolute 10/10. i was soooo looking forward to crying like a little baby and regretting every decision ive ever made 😖😖the plot is basically like the la la land epilogue, 96  cafe scene, side b dream scene, all mixed in one and made into an hour long chapter rather than just a small scene. the scenes i just mentioned are one of my favourite moments of each movie, so a film like this, where the entire plot is around this topic should’ve been perfect for me. but why didn’t it work out for me? \n\nthe movie i find this most similar to is 96. 2 childhood sweethearts reconnecting after an incredibly long time, where one of them is married and one of them is just unable to move on. but in 96 i was rooting for them to succeed so bad, in past lives a part of me was almost hoping they didn’t work out. it’s not at all to do with the performances or the way the two leads were shown tho cos their chronic regret and love for each other was absolutely believable; i couldn’t help but feel bad for sung in every single scene, constantly stuck in this cycle of “what if it had worked out”, that too across 24 long years. but i think making the husband present through out the entire film made it so difficult for me to, idk bro difficult to root for anyone or WANT a certain event to happen. like in 96 i WANTED jaanu to not board that flight, i WANTED her to cheat on her husband, cos i didn’t KNOW who he was. i didn’t know her kids, i didn’t know how their relationship was, nothing. and i think the fact you didn’t know anything about her life that she’s living at home made it much easier to root for ram and jaanu to work out cos you don’t even THINK about the fact she has her own life now. to be completely fair it’s not like it’s good that i’m rooting for her to leave her husband and kids behind and that conflict is probably (tbf it literally is) one of the central themes of this movie but i just , i’m not interested in that yk? tbh i think i just went into this movie being very very close minded cos im realising now that the movie very clearly is NOT trying to make you root for nora and sung to work out , but the entire first half of the film feels like it’s trying to do just that. i guess it’s just being realistic? like if my childhood chellam came back into my life but she had a boyfriend it’s entirely unrealistic for her to cheat on him but like. it’s a movie yk i wanted to live in this fantasy world where the hopeless romantics end up winning. idek what im tryna say bro i guess the movie just didn’t go the direction i wanted it to go and that’s absolutely not the makers fault it jus wasn’t the movie for me \n\nhowever the movie is absolutely absolutely gorgeous. sounds phenomenal aswell im listening to the soundtrack rn n it’s literally making me reminisce about every talking stage ive ever had lmaoooo whats wrong w me bra. everytime i felt myself losing interest there would be the most beautiful shot of all mankind on screen n it would hook me again. the entire ferry scene was soooooo nice to look at. but yeah idk not a fan. again such a super duper beautiful movie tho maybe this warrants a rewatch when im in a mature place. idk .",
