    "review": "🥰🥰🥰\n\nwhat a fucking BANGER DUDE WTF !!!!! i’m SO mad i missed this in cinemas i was literally DEBATING GOING IDK WHY I DIDNT 😭😭 lowkey could’ve been a 10 if i did \n\nanyway i acc dk how to review cos there’s BARE stuff i wanna talk ab but ill do all the good stuff first \n\nif u saw the review i posted before yk i found reenu unIMAGINABLY BEAUTIFUL BRO WHAT THE HELL 😭😭😭 nah like at first when aadhi was moving to her i was ACC MAD LMAO i know i JUST said in raayan that i’ve never had a bigger crush on a woman than dushara but i was LYING dude MAMITHA NEE THAANDI EN KADHALIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIII  😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍 sorry i kinda lost my mind let me be serious \n\neveryone’s performances were INCREDIBLY good bro like everyone was just believable yk? like i don’t doubt for a SECOND that amal is a college student, or that sachin is that kinda lost in life but still surviving kinda guy, or that aadhi is a fat PRICK!! n this extends to all the side characters too, i could literally name every single actor bro the cast did their ting filming this movie hooolly. \n\nthe music too was SOOOO good, it was hearing kutty kudiye that acc made me want to watch the movie in the first place. the whole soundtrack is SUPER different to anything ive heard from south india before, it feels heavily us hip-hop inspired in a similar way to SaNa’s Mahaan. absolutely loved the bgm too , AND THE SCORE IS ON STREAMING !!! gonna rinse it during study sessions \n\nevery single aspect of this movie is excellently executed but the writing is the BEST part about it. it’s SO good at making you feel things; i was literally CHEESING when sachin n amal were first becoming bredrins w reenu and karthika and again at every moment where sachin was super haply I WAS LITERALLY SMILING CHEEK TO CHEEK TOO LMAO WHATS WRONG W ME . and the chemistry between reenu n sachin?!?!?!? good GOSH i cared SOOO MUCH about their relationship but i also didn’t think anyone was necessarily wrong; but more on that later. i didn’t cry cos the movie wasn’t really going for that but if it wanted to??? i could’ve been fucking BAWLING if they decided to take the ending in a different direction, BRO I WAS GETTING CLOSE when reenu rejected him n he was being all loner n stuff paavam pediyan 💔. ahhh man the happiness i felt whilst watching these guys fall in love 😭😭😭😭😭 nah it was so cute man especially that entire sequence when they were on the train. i was really hoping that reenu was gonna hear the things sachin was saying but in hindsight im SO glad they didn’t put that big turning point so early in the movie, everything that happens in between that scene and when he actually does propose was SUPER important in getting u to care about these characters n the relationships between them. genuinely after she rejected him i thought the movie was gonna go into a la la land winter kinda spiral which WOULDVE BEEN PEAK CINEMA but this route lowkey makes this peak comfort movie, sooooooo cute man. \n\nanyway i could glaze this movie for so long but its not a 10 for a reason, n i think thats cos of the final 30 or so minutes, cos i started to disagree w the message the movie was tryna make (i mean i think anyway i could be reading into it too much). after reenu rejected him it felt like the movie was tryna villainise her and victimise sachin. i feel like they were tryna make it seem like sachin was ENTITLED to a relationship w reenu just cos they were doing all these things together but if thats not what remus searching for then like, so be it innit?  especially when sachin kept arguing w her n saying like “oh cos my feelings mean that much to u don’t they” all that stupid shit it’s not like she was TRYING to hurt him she just wasn’t looking for that in life n i felt it was kinda gaslighty at that point? maybe agajn im looking into it 2 much but i jus felt like reenu was forced into loving him due to the forced absence rather than actually being at a stage in life where she wants a relationship. it felt like a very male fantasy kinda movie during that short section. that’s arguably my biggest gripe with the film but it absolutely does not overshadow all the AMAZING writing that comes before it. another SMALL gripe i have is aadhi’s final sequence chasing them to the airport. i LOVED the callback to the pepper spray that was a great pay off BUT the whole sequence in general felt kinda shoe horned in/ a massive disruption to the emotional flow the movie was going in. but again i can forgive that too. \n\nALSO THIS COULD BE THE BIIIIIGGGEEESSST REACH EVER BUT OMG when they go to karthika’s leaving celebration thing whatever it was (when reenu’s in the green dress why am i using that to label the scene lmao what’s wrong w me). when aadhi comes up to them n he’s like i need to talk to u guys AND THEN HES LIKE “i insist” AND THERES THAT WESTERN COWBOY MUSIC MOTIF IN THE BG, i SWEAR thats A RDR2 REFERENCE???? AGAIN BIGGEST REACH EVER BUT EVEN THE WAY HE GRABBED HUS HAND FELT SOOOOOO MUCH LIKE DUTCH WTF 😭😭\n\nanyway i loved the cinematography a LOT too like when the net bank team r doing their dance at the wedding n they kept crash zoom (idk if thats what its called) to show amal n sachins reactions that was so jokes. sorry to go off track but those 2 were so fucking funny the entire time man i can’t imagine how good this would’ve been in a cinema setting. lowkey tho i think it’s the chemistry they have + the way they deliver the lines which makes it so funny, the writing is the jokes itself is lowkey dry lmao. also what THE HELL LMAO why do mallus have that cadence when they talk?? ITS SOOO UNIQUE cos the individual words r very similar to tamil but their vocal inflections and jus the way they flow through sentences is SUUUPER different n recognisable its kinda cool. anyway back to cinematography yeah the movies super pretty the train sequence was a highlight for me, BEAUTIFULLY lit and graded n we never rly saw that kind of lighting anywhere else in the movie it was just a lot of plain day time shots. oh yeah when she’s in the kitchen crying n that bunny lamp he bought is the only visible source of light that was also suuuuuper pretty. bro ive been waffling for so fucking long basically the movie is so so so so soooo good. \n\nalso mamitha looks literally exactly like this other mallu girl i had a crush on at work n they’re similar age asw bro if i was still working there after i saw this movie i acc would’ve moved to her. mamitha my new crush most beautiful woman of all time 😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍 okay bye guys love u\n\nnah i lied i have some more this is tied w maharaja for best film of 2024 but they’re so wildly different i can’t even choose lmao. i put this movie in my ‘might save my life’ list n it absolutely did 🥰🥰!! also i rly hope i make a group of friends like this at uni, it felt bare reminiscent of when me maryam manvi soha were all super close BRO THAT ROADTRIP FELT LIKE I WAS JUST WATCHING OUR OWN TRIP BACK LMAO in fact sachin’s whole character felt suuuper relatable to me. love this movie man im never deleting the file for this movie cos there’s only like TWO torrents online n i had to wait BARE long for it to download. if anybody knows where i can get 4k print PUT ME ON!!!!! ok bye fr now love u",
