    "review": "working thru the niki list and i was lowkey scared to watch this movie cos EVERYONE and their MOTHER was gassing this movie up, i was worried it wouldn’t live up to the expectations especially watching it on my ones on my monitor instead of in the cinema. and lowkey i was right , watching this in a packed cinema with a load of other people feeling the same emotions as ne would’ve elevated the experience  by a lot but regardless this film was AMAZING !!!!\n\nim gonna quickly be a nerd but i found a dolby vision AND ATMOS PRINT OF THIS FILM WTF!!!!!!! i might asw have the dcp fam it was SOOOOOO HIGH QUALITY and DOLBY ATMOS???? HOOOOOLYYYY at first it didn’t feel that different cos it was just dialogue but IN THE CAVE SCENES??? BROOOO SO WORTH IT n i can’t even imagine what this would’ve sounded like in an atmos theatre bro holy shit. ok nerd para over \n\ni’ve never seen a movie LOCK IN so hard after the title card before. seeing the title card come 40 mins in already assured me that it was gonna be actual cinema but good GOSH the way everything ramps up after that title card (also I LOOOOOVED that the title card’s actually like part of the movie world i jus spent 5 mins tryna find the right terminology for it but that was super interesting imo). honestly bro the first 30 mins until they acc enter the guna caves i was getting super bored n i was wondering there’s no way everyone rated this movie so high. like i thought it was jus gonna be a cute slice of life movie and im SOO glad i went into the movie completely blind, and didn’t know anything about the history of the guna caves. niki woulda hated me bra i was trying so hard not to jus quit the movie but im SO GLAD i stayed !\n\nthe movie looks SO fucking good dude like the landscape shots were gorgeous , and everything was so saturated and had rich colours and was just really satisfying to look at. the music was lowkey my favourite part of the whole movie, and the FUCKING cave atmosphere sounds were SOO WELL DONE!!!! like what the FUCK bro everything felt airy and emphasised how isolated subhash was, it was so well made. anyways bra i always ramble about music n cinematography even tho i lowkey don’t have a clue what im talking about lol ALSO THE SCORE”S ON STREAMING WWWW\n\nalso holy shit bra when they were lowering kitten into the caves and they did those pov + snorricam shots that was SO anxiety inducing bro what the FUCK, added to the tension so much more. anyway the storytelling , although kinda predictable was REALLY REALLY REALLY well done in a way that completely excuses its slight predictability; you feel EVERY single emotion that it wants you to feel , like when they finally get subhash out i acc like got out of my chair and walked around a bit like it was SUCCHHH A RELIEVING MOMENT. also YOOOO FAM when subhash had the hallucination in the cave, first of all brilliant lighting  w that really harsh red back light but anyway when he got out and he sees HIMSELF from earlier bro that was SO FUCKING SICK WTF and the proper 0.5x kinda shot (idk if it’s called macro lens or wha) where it shows him calling out to them was sooo good asw. ALSO the flashbacks were super well placed, especially the one when subhash\t jumps into the lake or whatever and it transitions into him falling down the cave FUCK OFF SO SICK that was kinda expected but STILL IM SO GLAD THEY DID IT ! im lowkey just recapping the movie bro i need to learn how to properly write reviews lmao but anyway OH YEAH as soon as the whole lowering someone into the cave sequence started and they had all the people holding the rope i immediately  thought back to when they were practicing  for the tug of war and the ENTIRE time i was just waiting for the main crew to go pull the rope and it was SOOO satisfying when they finally did. i think what made it so much better was that they didn’t acc flashback to the tug of war, the movie just kinda expects you to remember which again made it feel even more satisfying when you get to make that connection yourself, rather than it being force fed to u, ygm? i like when movies don’t treat the audience like they’re loosu pediyans\n\nalso it’s probably cos a lack of signal or something but why didn’t they give kitten a walkie talkie when he got lowered into the cave i feel like that would’ve made things much easier . i know i keep saying kitten but u guys know who  i mean lmao im writing on my MacBook and this punde autocorrect is so annoying to keep fixing. lowkey more like an 8.5 but that's why the heart is there. also stayed up til like 5 to watch this movie fam wtf \n\ngonna do a journal entry n then watch penguin ep3 bye guys love u",
