    "id": "diary-272",
    "title": "96",
    "releaseYear": 2018,
    "releaseDecade": "2010s",
    "director": "C. Prem Kumar",
    "language": "Tamil",
    "movement": "Tamil Romance & Melodrama",
    "runtimeMinutes": 158,
    "watchedDate": "2024-10-13",
    "loggedDate": "2024-10-13",
    "rating": 5.0,
    "isRewatch": true,
    "isLiked": true,
    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "rath try not to use letterboxd as a journal challenge (IMPOSSIBLE) \n\n💔💔💔💔💔💔 i fucking CRIED AGAIN LOOOL i had a dream ab this movie like two weeks ago and ever since then ive been itching to watch it so bad. so annoying how hard it is to find this online without paying but anyway\n\nidk why but i don’t think there’s another movie in the world that im so emotionally attached to. of course la la land is my favourite piece of media ever and nothing will change that, but that movie is more of a stylised take with more focus on the progression of each individual character’s lives, whereas 96 feels like a personal and intimate portrayal of the relationship between these two people. lowkey that was a load of waffle but im tryna say 96 is more personal than la la land is lol \n\nit’s been close to 3 years since ive last seen this movie and im so glad i waited as long as i did, because it amplifies all the emotions in the movie way more when you can’t fully remember them. the first time i watched this movie i didn’t even know it was a sad movie lmao i was just in my vjs era and going thru his whole filmography, bro i started watching this whilst eating dinner w my family 😭😭😭 i absolutely wasn’t expecting it to make me as sad as it did. but anyway i feel like im a hopeless romantic, and these types of stories where people are in an ‘impossible relationship’ feel SOOOOO relatable to me. i mean the entire movie i kept imagining myself in that scenario and BRO it made the lump in my throat start from the MIDDLE OF THE MOVIE bro it wasn’t even THAT SAD YET WTF 😭 n from then on every sequence (cafe scene, seeing the airport from the train, at ram’s house) just built on that sadness more and more and more until that SOUL CRUSHING ending. the concept of the movie as a whole is just really sad cos these people are so clearly meant for each other but fate forbade them from being together so many times. it’s the whole “if one thing went different” thats such a haunting feeling and is lowkey the backbone of the entire second half of the movie, especially during the cafe scene. it was similar to the dream scene in side b, building up all that hope and then bringing you crashing down back to reality. gosh i love when movies explore that feeling cos i always find myself thinking ab those “what could’ve been” situations i need to stop\n\nits really hard to review this movie cos the story is unimaginably simple but SO powerful at the same time and that’s helped massively by trisha and vjs’ potentially career-best performances. (defo trisha’s best , vjs is debatable). so much of the story is told not through dialogue but by the characters’ expressions; you can absolutely tell that ram’s a man who lives entirely within the past and is constantly haunted by it. his obsession with photography and wanting to freeze a moment in time feels so in line with his character and i just realised they never took any pictures during their time together. there’s probably some deeper meaning to that about him finally living in the present or something but idk it’s 4am and im tired lol. and you can practically FEEL the chronic regret coming from jaanu, especially when they’re talking ab the time ram went to the college to see her again. the entire movie you can see these characters treading the fine line between “im so happy im with you rn, but im so sad i cant be with you forever” and its so so painful to see. the chemistry between them is INCREDIBLE man, the whole story just feels like the word yearning personified. also after seeing past lives i appreciate this story so much more, past lives’ cinematography is the only thing it has on 96 (mainly due to its higher budget, 96 had an incredible vision that with a past lives level budget could be top 5 most beautiful movies ever) but anyway past lives got so much wrong in its retelling of this story (imo) but go read that review to see y i hated it so much lmao\n\nand the music is so so so so so painful man, govidh vasantha fr created magic w this soundtrack, in 2021 there were like 6 songs from the score in my top 100 most played. bro when iravingu theevai starts during the climax ???? FUCKED man  every song is just incredibly sad and you can feel your heart sink when the first few notes of each one starts. the placement of the songs also feel so perfect, especially iravingu theevai, vasantha kaalangal and every time the kaathale motif plays \n\ni lowkey might get bare personal after this (bro can there PLEASE be a close friends setting) so if u don’t know me pls fack off 🙏🏽🙏🏽🙏🏽\n\ni feel like im lowkey not saying anything in this review lmao mb ik we just had summer break but id do anything to have like 5 days to myself to like recalibrate fam,  first year has taken a HORRIBLE toll on me mentally n then bare stuff even outside of uni happened n it’s all jus HORROR timing bro i lowkey wanna rewatch side A cos that movie made me cry like never before but i also wanna watch good will hunting cos i think that kinda hopeful movie is exactly what i need to pull me out of my rut rn. slyly i think i should watch some happy movie like gang leader or the nice guys or something SORRY IM WAFFLING AGAIN MB !!! but anyway my favourite thing to do in the entire world is reminisce and live in the past and this movie is a painful reminder of how important it is to keep yourself grounded in the present but still man. i feel like ive been trying to say something this entire review but i jus can’t get it out okay now im lowkey just journalling holy shit lmao\n\noh yeah i’m also super excited to watch meiyazhagan now but ita genuinely gonna be impossible to find bra. they’re showing vettaiayan near me but im wondering if i should wait till i go back to ldn next week idk \n\nbye guys love u",
