    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "? \n\ni’m stuck between absolutely despising this ‘film’, and finding it creative and introspective (in a really shit way though) \n\nspoilers !\n\nthe films obviously trying to tell a story of child abuse but reversing the roles in an effort to be creative and whilst a lot of the concepts on paper sound, not interesting but unique and thought provoking, the experience of watching the film isn’t really enjoyable in any way at all. of course i don’t think a story about this topic is supposed to be ‘enjoyable’ but it felt like there was no real reason for anyone to watch this film. like you don’t get anything out of it \n\ni do think the sound design was phenomenal, that sort of droning/thumping sound during the middle of the film when sidney’s writing his memoir thing REALLY adds a lot to the tension, and the super loud, blunt footsteps too all these sounds make that moment super nerve wracking. and again in the bathroom when he’s being abused, only showing the audio and leaving the rest to the imagination again it was a clever (i feel so weird using a positive word about the film fucking hell) way to add onto that tension. \n\nnah icl bun reviewing this movie 😭😭😭 so meady and i get that it’s supposed to be shocking but it just felt like “look how edgy and dark my film is 🤯🤯” n all the reviews glazing it n calling it deep r so jarring y am i actually vexed 😭  ok no actually \n\ni will say the mum character was interesting n reflective of real scenarios like this, n this was most apparent during the bathroom scene. i like how there’s also an alternate interpretation where u look at the intro as the son thinking that sidney saying “those feelings are normal” is about the incest thoughts the son has. i like how the memoir thing is labelled confessions, as if to say sidney feels to blame for what happens. i like how in the memoir he even puts some of the blame on himself, it all feels accurate to what an actual abused child feels. even the title of the memoir, cocoon man, suggests that sidney feels like he can protect himself from the bad stuff happening around him but in the end he’s just a desperate and powerless ‘child’. there’s definitely clever metaphors in the movie and lowkey jus writing this review n thinking ab the different meanings js kinda warming me up to the movie but it’s still a massive pile of shit. i like how isaiah is shown as a super gaslighter n even the mother is shown as powerless in a way because she’s ignoring the abuse that’s going on cos she’s also scared \n\nok nah suck ur mum this movies so knacks yk i was watching incendies asw but one of my friends got home bare drunk n i had to look after her so i wanted to watch something quick before bed n i saw gnana’s review n got interested i regret it so much 😭😭 i should’ve jus finished incendies bra it’s 6.30 am rn tho my sleep schedules so cooked. lowkey coming out my super depression era which feels soooo good fam i can’t believe i was being such a cry baby in my reviews last week what a baby 😭😭😭😭😭 ok gn fr tho love u",
