    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "SOOOOOOOO CUUUUTE 🤭🤭🤭🤭🤭🤭🤭🤭 \n\ni remember i watched first 25 mins of this w my cousin like a month ago n then i stopped n i CANT BELIVE I DIDNT KEEP GOING BRO THIS IS A BANGER WTF 😭😭😭😭\n\nit’s also bare short asw n i lowkey wanted to see jaya spend more time w deepak’s family that was kinda cute , it was so wholesome seeing all the characters slooowly\nopen up and be all cheery and cute . like the grandma at the train station i looove how she’s initially a really cold like keeps to herself kinda woman but by the end she’s inviting phool into her house (N HER KITTYS SOO CUTE) and she’s giving her all this beautiful advice and WHEN AHE FINALLY TRIED HER DESSERT 😍😍!! n seeing jaya slowly integrate w all the diff ppl in deepak’s family was so adorable and seeing her bring a sort of light to the family despite the circumstances they’re in. n i loved how on a deeper level both of the women found who they were in life asw cos of the time they spent alone like the whole thing was just so happy man. bro the entire final 20 mins from when they find phool’s poster at the station i was CHEESING like a little baby bro SOOOOO CUTE 😭 ive said cute like 18 times this review but thats genuinely the best way to describe this movie bra it’s jus so so happy and i also really like how the main sort of issues they’re tryna tackle w the whole feminism thing is actually really serious , like when the grandma was talking ab when she’d be beaten but it’s all contrasted with this hopeful positive messages of independence and finding yourself and changing the stereotypical idea of what a woman is . despite its core message it never feels preachy , the whole thing is just a really fun ride. when jaya was falsely accused i was a little ☹️ but i KNEW she wasn’t a bad woman man bro even the side characters were rly well written in the movie , i really liked the girl jaya was besties w (forgot her name oops) and chottha too bro basically all the side characters were cool and cute 😭😭 also the music was sooooo cool and sajni is a banger but i couldn’t stop thinking about that stupid brainrot remix where it’s like “o skibidi re” 😭😭😭😭😭😭😭 i lowkey have nothing but good things to say about this movie man imagine i was ab to watch incendies asw that depressing ass movie faaaaacking hell . lowkey dk what else to say super funny OH YEAH ITS REALLYYYY FUNNY TOO bro fucking when jaya leaves the police station n he’s like “she’s gonna go far” n he says yeah that uni’s like 800km away 😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭 piss off lowkey worst joke ever but i was laughing out loud for like 20s straight. that cop character too i loved the transition he went through, i thought he was gonna be the main villain at first but that redemption arc he had for his climax scene 🤞🏽🤞🏽🤞🏽🤞🏽 peak cinema man i was grinning so hard that entire scene. AND YOOOO when prashad singh (whatever jaya’s ex husband was called) was like wb my money n the cop’s like is that a bribe ?!!? I SAID IT AT THE SAME TIME AS HIM BROOOOO i didn’t expect him to end up becoming one of my fav characters in the movie. the whole cast is just a bunch of super nice people u can’t help but smile the entire way thru. also jaya is super pretty bro \n\nbanger movie love u guys",
