    "isLiked": false,
    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "sooooo cute da \n\nis this ani’s best album ?!?!? 3 is the only one that comes close imo there’s not a SINGLE skip on the whole soundtrack that’s crazy \n\nfirst half is so so sooooo funny , my entire reels page is just young sk when he used to present audio launches n stuff and he was HILARIOUS , bro it’s absolutely wild to see his growth from playing as dhanush’s ‘sidekick’ in 3 to now cameoing in a vijay movie and grossing higher than a RAJINI multistarrer\n\nthe whole first hour of this movie captures that charm sk had in his early career SO well, every scene is hilarious and u can’t help but smile the whole way thru. sk and satish have great chemistry like the whole dumb and deaf thing was SO JOKES 😭😭😭😭 im such a kid but when owner and his kid kept farting in the school meeting i was giggling like a little baby bro omg . the romance w priya anand was lowkey really cute (but super rushed). icl a lot of the second half i was kinda annoyed that we just completely forgot ab her character . also i know i say this ab genuinely every actress ever born but ive had the biggest crush on priya for like 9 years now cos she looks exactly like the first girl i ever dated (she actually put me on to this album 🤯🤯) i lowkey fumbled her like 4 separate times from 2018-23 but at least it makes for a really interesting story\n\nsecond half unfortunately falls off SO hard imo , i get what they were going for with the whole finding a purpose thing but there were waaaaay too many things the film was tryna achieve all at once and that vaali flashback felt super duper out of place . it was interesting yes but taking us to an ENTIRELY new story with COMPLETELY new characters felt like it disrupted the flow of the movie so much . and ab priya again she lowkey disappears entirely for like 40 which was super annoying , another reason y i felt like the movie was tryna do too many things in a small runtime. \n\nagain the music is so fucking good bro and seeing it IN context makes it way more enjoyable too (was so funny finding out why it says unga aaya in the title track loool), velicha poove could very possibly be the BEST tamil song ever made it was my most listened to song in 2021 🤞🏽 idk y i keep dropping rath lore in these reviews mb guys \n\nreview over yap time again 😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭\n\ni can’t believe it took me this long to finally watch this movie bro there’s so much 2010’s tamil cinema that i’ve missed out on cos i was a whitewashed PRICK back then , i only started exploring our culture in like 2021 that’s such an L . i’m finally out my depression era what a wet wipe 😭😭 im finally caught up on most of my lectures bro i got a fucking email from the wellbeing dept asking if i was okay mentally cos my attendance was so low 😭 BRO HE SAID “i just need to know you’re okay” im not gonna KILL MYSELF DA WTF 😭😭😭😭😭😭 im gonna start watching bare of these ‘comfort’ movies from this time period cos everytime i hear a song from these movies it brings me sooooo much nostalgia , like as soon as i hear oh penne from vanakkam chennai i instantly go back to like summer year 6/7 it’s a great feeling . i think im gonna become a Whore i am sick and tired of being lonely",
