    "review": "icl i was SUPER excited to watch this even tho it’s not a romcom but ante sundaraniki director + nani THIS SHOULDVE BEEN SOOO GOOD\n\n- absolutely INCREDIBLE lighting , especially that interval fight scene was soooo gorgeous \n- score is insane too , the one when nani and pam meet for the first time ‘bottle cap n scooty pep’ was so cute but it’s genuinely like 15s long \n-  that one slow shutter fight scene 😍😍😍😍😍😍😍\n\ni still liked nani a lot in this movie but i much prefer him in his chill roles like ante and hi nanna, but that might jus be because of the movies im into rn . in tamil cinema there haven’t been any ‘chill’ movies , especially from the top heroes in AAAAAAGEESSSS bar like thiruchitramblam. literally like 2/3 months ago those dark massy action movies like raayan were ALL i was interested in but lately these easy going romcoms r all i wanna watch idk y ive had such a big 180  \n\nante sundaraniki made me care about the characters SOOOO much and i was really hoping for something similar here , but it didn’t work so well this time :( i think vivek is a PHENOMENAL director (from the 2 movies i’ve seen lol) cos a lot of the visual choices he makes are beautiful, but the writing in this movie wasn’t good enough imo. \n\nhonestly the 3 hours didn’t FEEL like 3 hours at all, but looking back i realised after the interval , lowkey nothing really happened 😭😭😭 the final 30 mins feel a tad long \n\nmild spoiler !!!\n\nbro when pam started explaining the eega plot THAT WAS SOOOOO CUTE and then when he was like “so who’s nani?” n she was like “you’re nani” like that’s actually year 4 level of writing but it’s SOOO CUTE LOL i love when movies talk about the main actor as if they’re an actor in the movie world too \n\nalso the dad character was really annoying every scene he was in felt like it made the movie worse 😭😭\n\ngenuinely completely forgot the name of it but gonna watch the movie athreya made before ante next !",
