    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭 gosh i love this movie so much bra\n\nicl i had to watch like 30 mins of it in tamil cos my\nmum didn’t understand anything nani has the WORST tamil dubbing artist of ALL time bro there is NO SIMILARITY BETWEEN THEM 😭😭 ALSO in the tamil version during young nani’s song its kamal hassan’s pictures in the bg instead of chiranjeevi THATS SO COOL WTF i just checked the mallu version n it has mohanlal W localisation 😍😍\n\nwhen u rewatch it’s way easier to catch all the little jokes n references n it made the movie EVEN more enjoyable bro i rly love the vibe this film has \n\nalso WTF why is half the album jus NOT ON APPLE MUSIC??? THE SPOTIFY VERSION HAS LIKE 3 EXTRA SONGS N THEYRE ALL GOOD SOMGS ASW IM SO VEXED , thera theesindhi MIGHT be the best telugu song ive ever heard \n\nalso i never deeped sundar is literally me bro i LOVE LYING (small lies tho) n i hate facing my problems head on 😖😖 \n\nnani is actually hilarious bro like HILAAAARIOUS now im super excited to see athreya’s previous movie . didn’t like saripodhaa that much but its an action movie n im not in my action bag rn anyway so we’ll see 🫣🫣\n\nalso i think there should’ve been a post credit scene where joshua gets blown up and killed but that’s jus me\n\nok bra i keep adding more stuff after i posted this but what did they FILM THIS WITH BRO???? its SOOOOOO BEAUTIFUL my fav scene HOLY SHIT NO I LIED okay \n\nSPOILERS!!!!!!\n\n- when they go to that friends wedding in kerala that entire chapter is beautiful but SPECIFICALLY after the wedding’s over and they’re on that kayak and it’s blue hour, that scene is ENGRAINED in my mind and has been ever since i first watched it. bro i’ve rewatched that specific scene like 4 times since  i first saw the movie 😭 it’s such a stunning blue and i LOVE how their kayak stays stationary and everything passes by them. i still can’t tell if their boat’s moving or not bro there’s probably a bit of visual symbolism in there ab how they’re kinda frozen in time at that moment (but i’m not smart enough to explain that lol) \nAND the shot straight after where they’re inside a boat n inside is warm lighting compared to blue outside NOT JUST that but playing dialogue from a different scene over it , it felt SOOOO perfect. like showing us that there’s this slight change in the way they’re behaving around each other n there’s a little bit of tension , n then playing dialogue over it to more explicitly show what’s actually changed between them. idk those 2 shots are my favourite in the entire film , i wish i was better at analysing film bra i love that scene so much. the score at that point was sooo good too i wish vivek released it. unless he dropped it on spotify n not apple music wasteman\n\n- when she asks to marry him and he steps out the car and he’s like stationary but ‘floating’ backwards and all the lights r turning on by themselves and doors opening themselves and stuff, the same thing happens when leela gets back home too i LOOOVE when movies become a little fantastical n show us exactly what the characters r feeling at that point in time \n\n- EVERY scene inside leela’s office is BEAAUUUUUTIFULLY lit, but my fav is just before they go to america n they’re ab to execute this plan everything in this GOORGEOUS orange hue and the set is all orange and green COMPLEMENTARY colours bro i wanna learn colour theory so bad. imagine rewatching la la land after fully understanding colour theory must be so insane \n\n- the scene when they’re all on a table n it’s spinning around i jus learned thats inspired by spike lee thats SO cool dude i alr spoke ab that in my first review tho",
