    "isLiked": true,
    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "i find reviewing movies easier than journalling bro i haven’t done an entry in over a month im actually SO cooked mentally it’s insane . i think thats y i like doing life updates on here lmao it’s less intimidating than tryna do a full on entry anyway yap over \n\nMASSIVE departure from the type of movies i’ve been watching lately idk y but it felt like this movie was calling for me looool. also this movie indirectly changed my life \n\nthe 151 scene is still SOOOO good bro and the FUCKING TUNED AUTO LMAOOOO BRO 10K RPM?!?!?!? WTF😭😭😭😭😭😭😭 i don’t watch a lot of action movies but these r by far the BEST fight scenes ive EVER seen bro HOOOLY SHIT. i LOVE LOVE LOOOOOVE the way they move the camera cos it’s very chaotic but not in a way where u can’t follow the action; like in saripodhaa i didn’t like the fights much cos u cant rly see whats going on but here the camera movements work with the choreography and makes for some SUUUPER fun fight scenes . icl in tamil movies u can always see that the actors miss each other on purpose but BRO NOT AT ALLLLL here , EVERY hit felt like it had weight behind it they’re SOOOO well choreographed dude\n\nmy fav fight scene FOR SURE was near the end when dev’s at the hotel n he shoots the fireworks into the crowd , BRO ALREADY it was hard cos the fireworks gave me mega ghost of tsushima vibes n the SCORE HOOOOOLY i love how they used a more acoustic , almost relaxing score for that scene compared to what you’d expect . the contrast w what’s acc on screen is SOOOOO cool i loved it . but anwyay when u see dev get all surrounded and then THE HIJRAS COME IN BRO THATS FUCKING CINEMA 🔥🔥🔥🔥🔥🔥🔥  i loved their costumes too, especially when they acc start fighting n they started spinning and the dresses do that thing (on my life idk how to describe it i sound so stupid) \n\nanyway i forgot how TRAUMATISING dev’s childhood was bro WTF ?????? i was struggling to finish that scene bra that’s INSANE 😭😭 but it gave the fight scene w rana SOOOOOO much emotional stakes and i love how it showed us how he got those burn marks on his hands , n then u realised that he lied about it every time someone asked ab it that was cool. anyway the rana right was so good but lowkey the actual climax fight scene felt kinda underwhelming in comparison, cos even tho baba is the BIG bad the emotional conflict is still more directly associated w rana ygm. but i think dev knew this too cos that fight scene is waaaayyyy shorter. HOWEVER !!! the climax fight VISUALLY was STUNNINNGGGGGG bro whatever painting that was on the wall is actually jaw dropping bro and when they acc start fighting and they’re jus silhouettes against that red art 😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍😍 unbelievable . and the caustics on baba at the start were so pretty bro everytime i see caustics in a movie im actually in awe \n\nlowkey i reread this review and it’s actually ass but i need to keep my mind occupied with something so im gonna add an extra para 😍😍 dude the CINEMATOGRAPHY HOOOOOLY FACK i love how every single shot theres like several layers to the composition i learned that thats called dirtying the frame and i haven’t stopped using that phrase since lmao but EVERY shot , outside of the main focus point there’s so many other things happening asw it’s incredibly detailed and makes the film so visually interesting , not to sound generic but it makes the city feel real ygm . actually im yapping so hard bro this is the worst review ever \n\nalso dev patel super leng shobitha unimaginably gorgeous also i didn’t realise how UP DEV WAS BRO WTF ????? 😭😭😭 like i knew he was popular but half a MILLION members is BARES NO??? lowkey made me feel so proud cos a few of the cast members were south indian asw bro BABA WAS IN FUCKING JAILER LOOOOL",
