    "review": "mild spoilers\n\njesse’s a stronger man than me bro if that was me i would’ve cried and killed myself 17 times\n\ni love rewatching movies that i didn’t like the first time i watched them , this was such a cute movie and im glad i revisited it . i wasn’t expecting to like it cos it’s literally ENTIRELY dialogue but it’s FLIPPING GOOD WRITING bro \n\nthe conversations felt so natural and EVERY convo was insightful and interesting and actually made me like think about it yk? like there weren’t really any filler lines here, i really wanna have a convo like these guys do but i am not NEARLY as intelligent or well spoken as them 😭😭 but all the convos felt meaningful and explored so many different topics and i liked how they always had differing opinions but were teaching each other new things ab their perspectives yk it was really sweet \n\ni loooove that one scene where they pretended to talk to their friends to tell each other their deeper \n‘insecurities’ or fears or whatever i’ve done that a couple times before it’s so cute \n\n“i like to feel his eyes on me when i look away” i would’ve proposed to her that SAME day \n\ni feel like the entire film has a subtle feeling of melancholy , especially when they realise that this connection they’re building could last for all but a night . i absolutely looooooved the scene on the pier restaurant or wtvr it was when they were dancing around the topic of keeping in contact you can feel both people slyyyly holding their guard up and saying things they might not really believe in like “why does every relationship need to last forever anyway” idk i forgot what she said but every line they said had a smallll sense of regret / doubt to it and i looooved it so much . i was kinda getting the same feeling i did from 96 and if the movie wanted to it could’ve DESTROYED me w the ending \n\nalso their chemistry is ridiculous bro . i alr spoke ab the dialogue but even physically all their expressions and their slight nervousness talking to each other and their quick glances at each other like in the listening booth aaaaaa its so cute man . \n\nthese one takes are RIDICULOUS btw bro that tram scene was like SIX MINS LONG BRO ZEEEROOOO CUTS???? that’s FUCKED bro i’m lowkey repeating myself bares but at times it felt like they were jus improvising their lines like it didn’t even feel like written dialogue \n\ni loooove love man im tryna make my logs less personal n sappy but ive been longing for a connection like this my entire life ! i wish i was more outgoing n more open to talking to people not even jus in a romantic way but jus in general i wish i was able to make friends more easily . but also in a romantic way lol the love in first sight trope is done SOOOOO well here i feel like in tamil movies it can seem stalkery but they showed the excitement of this kinda romance SO WELL dude . are soulmates real ?!?!? idk ill let u guys know when ive found mine in 5 years we pray 🙏🏽🙏🏽\n\nim excited to watch the sequel cos theyre super cutie putie but lowkey i hope they go thru the most devastating break up of all man kind (nobody is allowed to be happy when im still single)",
