    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "the cinematography is different but it’s SOOOOOOO GORGEOUS THIS TIME EVEN BETTER THAN THE FIRST TWO !! i’ve lowk lost my ability to write ab cinematography like idk how to describe how the film looks besides jus saying it looks beautiful 😭 like something ab the way the shots are framed are so appealing here , i love all the scenes where the cameras still and we’re just shown a really pretty landscape or when jesse stefanos and patrick are talking ab his new novel , or when they’re all playing football together , or even when they’re watching the sun set behind the mountain like it’s just a really gorgeous movie . bro i could actually list every single scene before they get to the hotel like this is actually a gorgeous beautiful stunning movie . i really like how it’s shot on digital this time but still has some of the qualities of film like the grain is so pretty dude \n\nthe score is soooo beautiful this time !!! a lot of it is just the same motif w different variations but i really like it i added it to my journalling playlist . might try learn it on guitar it’ll defo be easier than city of stars 😭😭😭\n\nalso im in AWE AGAIN by these long takes bro some of these scenes r like 7 8 mins long with no cuts how do you even memorise that much dialogue bro . good gosh \n\nspoilers 😛😛😛the movie itself tho ??? idk how i feel about it like maybe it was going for a realistic approach that true love isn’t a real thing and people always fall out of love and whatever and maybe im jus being a naive baby but i think the movie was trying too hard to push the message that the love and connection shown in the first 2 movies is unattainable yk? holy shit bro longest sentence ever mb but yeah obviously arguments happen and people fight and whatever but it feels like jesse n celine r really different to the other 2 movies , especially jesse . he keeps bringing everything back to sex and when celine was being vulnerable he kept blowing it up / taking the piss out of her (don’t get me wrong i do think celine was over dramatic) like it wasn’t an enjoyable watch yk? a lot of the deep philosophical conversations they had in the first movie have turned into “would u still ask me to get off the train now” or “do you think we’ll be together forever” like all these “can’t win” q’s that jesse called them . and the ending was really annoying for the opposite reason like that massive argument they just had and they got back together just like that ?!?!? and thru SEX again like she mentioned several times that she doesn’t wanna be seen for jus her beauty and the whole feminism idea so it just felt kinda contradictory that ending \n\nahhh idk i feel conflicted cos at the same time celine and jesse were both right for feeling the things they did it jus felt like they wouldn’t hear each other out . i think i would’ve been happier if they really did break things off cos the movie spent the last 30 40 mins showing that these guys aren’t right for each other only to go back on ALL of that like i can’t tell if the movies tryna say that “marriages r problematic” or that “arguments are natural” \n\nlowkey this review is super yap n im gonna rewatch this eventually but idk what the message of the movie is n its also 4am i am hungry and very tired 🔥🔥\n\nngl i acc deleted this app today GOD knows why but movies have been the only thing distracting me from life lately bro like i have no other way to escape my anxiety bro wtf !!! like film is probably the thing im most passionate about in my entire life and i loooove being able to post these reviews n read other people’s it’s bare comforting . sorry to get bare emotional out of nowhere lmaooo im so grateful that i have this app tho i found one of my best friends of all time niki thru this app dude !!! thats crazy",
