    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "one of the things i’m probably most proud of about myself is being from eelam \n\nthis doc was HARD to get thru man i started tearing up like 20 mins in, honestly this short vid feels like it’s massively changed my perspective on everything like how am i supposed to look at my parents the same now that i’ve actually SEEN what they’ve gone thru bro. cos my entire life ive heard the stories they’ve told me but now seeing video evidence it kinda made it click a little more if that makes sense. im so happy my parents and their relatives are living happier lives abroad now but i can’t help but think ab everything they’ve gone thru to get to where they are. my dad was even captured at one point (God knows how he escaped and im absolutely not gonna ask him to retell that story bro that’s acc lifelong trauma) n its  like bro i cant even BEGIN to think of how scary it would be to LIVE through this bro wtfff\n\nalso it’s absolutely insane that theres video evidence of actual war crimes and the UN or anyone at all refuse to acknowledge it bro i was so angry seeing the state propaganda clips, they actually failed us man\n\nwhen i was younger i used to be ashamed of being sri lankan like i hated my skin colour and my long surname and so much about me but ive grown to love and embrace my culture more than anything and it makes me incredibly proud to see so many other eelam tamils making it big in the uk like avinaas and shini (presenter on big big cbbc???? faaacking hell) . even sometimes when i talk to indian tamils i speak in the indian dialect but icl fuckkkk that fam never again. i only know a few other eelam tamils on this app but i love u guys 🫶🏽 everytime i go the maveerar naal ceremony thing its such an amazing feeling seeing ALLLLL these other people from the same background as me with the same struggles all coming together to remember everyone who wasn’t as lucky as us. fuuuuuck bra im tearing up AGAIN \n\nalso my parents met each other during the civil war cos my dad helped my mums family flee thats a love story and a half bro mani ratnam where u at \n\nfree eelam forever 🐅 🫶🏽 man i originally had a p long review written for this but i started crying halfway thru writing it so i deleted it 🔥🔥 the silly reviews will be back next movie \n\ni rly wanna watch a romcom or sumn now to lighten the mood but its 3am rn why did i choose to watch this now lol",
