    "review": "this is one of my favourite love stories ever \n\ni didn’t think i’d cry again but good gosh 😭 i acc have tears in my eyes writing this review loool\n\nmild spoilers !\n\nthis feels more like a poem than it does a movie , like it feels really old fashioned (in the best way possible!) the romance and chemistry between manu and priya feels so so real , and even tho they never show us how they met each other and started to like each other it doesn’t even feel necessary because as a couple they feel so realistic . i love how priya’s fondness for the calm sea directly contrasts with manu’s adrenaline rush he gets from speeding (he’s literally me lol) and the way rao used this to move the plot forward (making us think it acc was manu speeding and causing that accident) was really well done imo. \n\nthe music is far and away my fav thing ab the film it used to be toss up between that and the visuals but bro??? 6 months later this soundtrack and score has only gotten better bro genuinely i think the duology’s score is top 3 movie scores of ALL time (along with la la land n maybe 96). and the music ??? kanmareya kaade is one of the best songs made EVER OF ALL TIME BRO it’s my most listened to song this year i need help 😭💔 also YOOOO she’s singing olave olave (my SECOND favourite song) IN THE TAPE SHE MADE FOR MANU??? YOOOO\n\nbut even besides the score and soundtrack , even the sound design is used a narrative device and it’s so well done . when they’re about to meet at the visiting room for the first time there’s this rly loud obnoxious ticking sound and it creates so much tension but as soon as they make eye contact ?? everything drowns out , the ticking becomes a really faint pleasant echo and it’s just the two’s voices you can hear and nothing else . that was so beautiful and it happens AGAIN when he’s about to listen to the tape and the sound of everybody working around him gets muffled and idk i just loooove love looove when movies put us in the pov of the character and they did it so well in those 2 scenes . \n\nalso when he chose the blue thread cos she said she likes the blue wall 💔💔💔 and all those little details like kathe and the 🤞🏽 makes their love feel even more real \n\ni have to mention the ending again bro that’s one of the best edited parallel sequences ive EVER seen bro i mentioned in first review asw but when they pour the cashews wtvr on priya n then it transitions to manu punching soma n the cashews r still there 😭😭😭😭🙏🏽 holy cinema \n\nalso the whole idea of the tape is so so sweet man . i’ve started recording tapes to myself cos i haven’t been journalling enough . idk why but when prakash was like “i hid this cassette from them” i almost started crying AGAIN i love how the cassette almost feels like it’s own character and they even made it play into the title of the movie too \n\ni could acc write for ages ab this movie i have sm more bullet points in my notes loool is it time for a side b rewatch ?!?!? paarpom \n\n“for me you are the sea” i am going to kill myself !!!\n\nnow i have the most depressing loser top 4 ever omfg i need a happy cool movie to put in there 😭😭😭",
