    "review": "- so pretty cinematography\n- score is goooorgeous i was kinda getting 96 vibes from it\n- when he stood up for her against that rich lady she spilled wine on 🥰🥰 i’m glad she had a redemption arc at the end tho that was sweet \n\nAAAAAA N THEN HE BOUGHT HER THE TEXTILES BOOK THING and her BIRTHDAY GIFT ??????? BRO I STARTED CHEESING SOOOO HARD ESPEC WHEN HE WORE IT TO WORK AWWWWWW\n\ni looooove how slowly the tension builds between them , like u can see him asking her more n more ab her life n checking in on her when she’s at the village n she’s still being like closed off cos maybe she feels like she isn’t “allowed” to have convos w him or maybe im reaching lol idk . all the subtle physical touches between them too oooooo\n\nlowk tho u do have to wonder if he rly was “in love w her” considering he didn’t even rly know her outside of the work environment like she’s jus being bare nice to him cos she’s his maid but what would their relationship be like if that power dynamic wasn’t there yk. it was still p cute tho i love movies ab love and i love it even more when its some type of forbidden love , but at the same time i like that it took a realistic approach n didnt make her ditch everything to be w him yk. like she had control of her own choices in the movie and ended up pursuing her textiles passion yk \n\nim lowk not smart enough to talk ab the class dynamics n im bare sleepy rn but 🔥 cute movie . slyly i haven’t even been enjoying movies like that lately or even writing reviews bruh im gonna log deathly hallows part 2 n then disappear for AGES (2 days) ok bye gn love u",
