    "review": "they played RUSHES IN THE SOUNDTRACK WTFFFF THATS LITR MY FAV FRANK SOMG OF ALLLLL TIME !!!! they acc played a lot of endless on here bro i absolutely adore that album its better than blonde imo . whole soundtrack banger but i couldn’t help but feel like the music was what made it so enjoyable\n\ngorgeous STUNNING jaw dropping cinematography bro aiiiyooooo these colours and the aspect ratio changes and the lighting ?!?!?!? bro that neon lighting was CRAAAAZYYYY i love how this movie looks. all those 360 shots inside the car was so cool i wonder how they did that \n\nbro all these american movies make the country look SO pretty dude all these late night drives n those scenes with luke and emily it’s so beautiful 😭 im so jealous man america 2026 is happening whether the guys are on it or not #solotravellingera \n\ni really love these life movies like coming of age or slice of life whatever they’re called . like this, didi, hridayam these kinds of movies feel so comforting to watch\n\nand of course the performances were absolutely incredible, the father was one of the more interesting characters cos i had this strange resentment for him in the first half but his vulnerability n change in the second half rly made me warm up to him i started to feel really bad for him too. especially emily too i feel like she could say w just her facial expressions and most of her quiet scenes were what connected w me the most \n\nok this bit isn’t even about the movie im lowk jus journalling icl tho i haven’t been connecting w these english movies as much as i have w south indian ones yk, bro i don’t even listen to english MUSIC nowadays 😭 was driving w my boys the other day n obvs they’re not tamil so we were listening to english songs n i was lowkey like damn 😭😭😭 someone put on aasa kooda rn bra (i did n they loved it 😄) \n\ni’ve lowk been feeling more distant from my family lately what w uni and other stuff asw so a lot of this movie hit kinda hard for me, i wish i was closer w my dad n sister sometimes. idk how to explain it but sometimes when my parents speak to me i jus feel kinda mad at them even tho they LITERALLY DIDNT DO ANYTHING and it annoys me everytime cos i love them obviously they’re my flipping parents but there’s jus this inner anger n idk where it comes from. the scene where luke goes to colombo hurt me a loooootttttt man that was hard to get thru. i can’t really explain why bro icl a lot of the emotions this movie made me feel idk where they even came from. good movie fr i wish i hadn’t started big short before tho might’ve enjoyed it more\n\nmy entire life ive had this deep yearning to be someone im not and for some reason this movie rly triggered that feeling for me . i guess it’s kind of in a good way but that sequence where he really kinda ruins his own life rly reminded me of what im doing rn like im picking up so many bad habits n i feel like im straying further n further away from the person i journal about being like . term 1 was a terrible time for me but term 2 rly flipped that on its head n i finally feel like im starting to find ‘my people’, like people are actively reaching out to me n inviting me to places and it makes me so happy but it’s all such a strange feeling im not used to this at all 😭 anyway anyway ive wanted to write ab the whole wanting to be someone else thing so bad but i can never find the words to express it properly bra . what the fuck brav i’m not tryna turn this app into my flipping journal again lmaooo bye guys love u ! i was supposed to sleep an hour ago FAAACK😛\n\ndidnt cry but i had a lump in my throat n idk why but the scene where the father comforts emily’s cat was one of the most emotional scenes for me 😭😭😭 also that’s the director’s real cat ! so cute kitty 😍",
