    "review": "hallo guys \n\nsuch an adorable movie , loved how innocent and pure they showed the friendship between siva and sekar , and with his teacher too the first hour and a half was quite sweet but at the same time there’s this undertone of melancholy when they take u out of the eyes of the children and show us the struggle the village as a whole is going thru \n\nbeautiful gorgeous amazing cinematography bro all the wide shots were 😍😍😍 i think the best word to describe the way this movie looks is atmospheric , i love how still the camera is sometimes to let us just soak in the views of the nature yk . gorgeous movie da also the black n white scenes 😍😍😍😍😍😍 \n\nsanthosh narayanan?????? SANTHOSH NARAYANAN????? SANAAAAAAAA YEN CHELLAKUTTYYY I LOVE YOU 😩😩😩😩🫶🏽🫶🏽🫶🏽🫶🏽🫶🏽🫶🏽 HOW DOES HE DO IT EEEEEVERYYYTIME DUDE oru oorla raja??????? MMMMMM 😍😍😍 ITS SO GOOD DUDE i love the instruments this guy uses like incorporating all the sounds of the animals and lorries n all HIS MYSIC IS SO UNIQUE !!! and “vaazhai’s surprise” such a soothing song asw man . anyway i knew the soundtrack was gonna be incredible but the SCORE !!! the SCOOOOOORE DAI SANA EPDI DA 😭😭😭😭😭 so so so beautiful bro all of nikhila’s themes were gorgeous and a lot of the strings for the more tragic scenes was sooo well done too . EVEN THE LIKE BREEZY MUSIC thru the first hour was so like 😄 nice cutie putie score \nhe’s doing a concert in the uk this summer but i lowk don’t have anyone to go with faack im not tryna go on my ones 😭\n\ni didn’t wanna say it but i have to say it nikhila is beautiful n having a crush on ur school teacher is so real #literallyme\n\nalso the child actors were incredible \nkarnan next ! i’m lowk getting a massive urge to rewatch pariyerum again . karuppi and rayil vida polaama has been on REPEATTTTT !!! \n\noh yeah and this being a real event in mari’s life? insane man he deserves all the praise he gets \n\nsong of the week is uravu - sean roland and vaa rayil vida polaama by sana\nAND “ORU OORLA RAJA” BY SANA BAAAANGERRR",
