    "isLiked": false,
    "isDiaryLogged": true,
    "review": "SUUUUUPPPERRRR BAANNGEERRRR !!! \n\ndid NOT expect to cry cos of this movie 😭 the rumours are true guys this is far n away the best tamil movie of 2025 (ive seen like 3 lol), felt like the meiyazhagan of this year\n\ni dont even know how to start this review bruh there’s SO MUCH I HAVE TO SAY\n\ncan’t even begin to describe how cute and wholesome this was bro i must’ve said ‘aww’ and like been CHEESING SMILING LIKE 100 TIMES THRU THE MOVIE BRO ITS SOOSOSOOOOO CUUUTEEE!!! unbelievablely funny too bro like the dialogues the facial expressions body language EVERYTHING BRO the comedy is written so well. n by far the funniest character was MILU LMFAAOOAOAOOA BRO HES SOO OFUNNY n this is his DEBUT??? bro what a debut from him AND from the director too (his role was done so well too, bro this guy’s gonna become something big)\nBUT YEAH milu does that kinda like unexpected humour SOOOOO WELL bro like the onam scene or the dog reveal or the mammutiya dance BRO ALMOST ALL HIS SCENES MAN\n\nbut for as funny as the film is its flipping EMOTIONAL asw man, like i thought it was jus a chill silly movie didnt think i was gonna CRY WTF 😭the whole family dynamic was super believable, espec all of nithu+sasikumar’s scenes bro that father-son dynamic felt wayyyyy too relatable . but even besides that all the relationships in the movie are just so pure and loving like you actually cant help but smile the entire time, a lot of ppl have said it but this movie really just feels a massive long warm hug n it never lets you go until the end. anyways the dementia subplot 💔 ruined me man i was fr tearing up on call bro if i watched this on my ones i think i would’ve started bawling but i had to maintain aura . that subplot felt bare relatable too man i became such a bum in term 1 after grammy passed away but im FUCKING #LOCKEDINNNNN NOW \n\nthere were no subs so that + the eelam accent meant we had to keep rewinding a couple times , that AND the fact we kept laughing over the dialogue LOL THIS MOVIES SO FUNNY MAN I LOVE IT !!! didn’t affect my enjoyment or how invested i was at all tho \n\nSOOOO many comfort actors here , ramesh thilak (i LOVE him), bagavathi , elango , i rly wish samuthirakani was here\nicl i kept forgetting ab the entire cops catching the terrorists storyline EVERYTIME bro the family were just sooo likeable n charismatic, but it did have a great payoff \n\nalso DID SASIKUMAR SAY PUNDAMONE LMAOAOAOAOAAOOAOAAOA THAT WAS SO JOKES 😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭😭\n\nULTIMATE comfort movie man, had stats exam in the morning n i was genuinely getting touched up and tortured and killed the entire 2 hours bra pure maths on thursday is gonna assault me so bad 😭 but this movie ahad everything i needed to forget ab all that stress bruh, so glad i watched this tn\n\nmillion dollar studios man. what a FUCKING PRODUCTION HOUSE BRO LOVER , GOOD NIGHT , TOURIST FAMILY SOMEBODY STOPPPP THEMMMMM 😭 happy ending teaser was genuinely incredible asw n i cant wait for once more either .  let me get another manikandan movie tho wld\n\nkural 😍😍😍😍😍 absolutely stunning n her and nithu’s romance track was ADORABLE\ni love how u can hear nithu’s mallu accent slip in sometimes that was so funny\n\nim v sad i missed seeing this in cinemas but movie night w niki so whateva 😛😛 was still a lot of fun \n\nanyways free eelam foreva!!! 🐅🫶🏽 man it was soooo cool seeing a movie where the characters speak like ME bro like when simran said vadivu by accident BRO THATS LITR THE SAME REACTION ALL MY INDIAN FRIENDS HAVE WHEN I SAY THAT LOOOOL \nbut again i genuinely smiled so hard hearing them speak MYYY DIALECT BRO EELAM WE UUUPPPPPPPP \ni know its politically v controversial n lowk would’ve got the movie banned but i would’ve loved to hear a nod to eelam or somethiiinggg but they fled to “escape the problems at sri lanka” which is CLOOSEEE ENOUUUGHHH  \n\nsean roldan score was great again but album wasn’t as good as his 2 manikandan ones imo \nloved seeing simran get a lead role too bro kollywood has a mega problem w getting rid of actresses once they turn like 30+ but pairing youngsters w old heroes like i will NEVER get over vikram-dushara in VDS bro ts was DISCOOSSTAANNGGG\n\nbut anyways banger padam bro go watch\n\nsong of the week is irrupen - vathshan",
