    "review": "i’m SO sorry i’m posting another serious review but my whole life has been bare stressful lately this is my only outlet 🙏🏽😭😭😭\n\nunfortunately i see myself in arun quite a bit and ive constantly been trying to change but it feels like ill never learn how to break down my childhood trauma , and the first time i saw this movie seeing that scene where his father walks around w another woman made me realise where a huge part of my flaws today come from . this part is lowk super tmi but anyway when i was younger my mum would always accuse my dad of having an affair n i always believed her n there would be arguments at home every single day and i think growing up in that kinda environment really changed the way i view love . i mean your home and your parents are your first impression of what love looks like and its supposed to be your safe space so when you spend ur entire childhood thinking that THAT is what love looks like its hard to break down those beliefs yk? \n\ni loved manikandan in this movie cos you can clearly tell that he hates that he is the way he is, but he just doesn’t know anything else . it feels like you can see a young arun in him that wants everything to feel secure and safe but he thinks the only way to achieve that is thru being controlling and jealous . thats not to say it’s not his fault at all tho arun is a terrible person but up until the ending it feels like he doesn’t even make an attempt to change either yk? i love that lover doesn’t try to glorify him at all (even if the audiences interpreted that way but yk what male indian viewers r like lol) , but instead it shows why he is the way he is, but that’s he’s still responsible for how he tries to improve \n\ni hope one day i can be like madan , don’t wanna repeat what i said in my last review but it feels like he’s arun’s foil character (GCSE ENGLISH LIT LFGGGGG) or his emotional mirror , and including the part ab him being like arun before but still managing to turn into this respectful calm guy was really great imo it shows that there’s potential for arun to break down his trauma and become a better person \n\nok anwyays im yapping time to sleep gn 😝😝😝",
