    "review": "DAN DAN DAN DANDANAKKA DAN DAN DAN DANDANAKKAAAA\n\nmost beautiful cinematography EVER EVEEERRR TOP 3 MOST GORGEOUS MOVIES OAT love howwww saturated the green was they made the forest look so rich yk all the inclusion of nature too all the animals insects n all \n\nalso ARR wow 😍\n\ncrazy how she instantly started defending dev at the wedding but the entire time veera is feeling guilty ab his stepsister like daammmmm why do they keep dehumanising veera’s tribe 💔\n\n“don’t show bad people in a good light” Wow what a way to criticise the media man i feel like the whole tribal vs urban thing has sommeeee type of link to caste like veera’s ppl r villainised just for surviving but im not smart enough to understand that \n\nfelt sooo similar to aditha karikalan n nandhini story in ponniyin selvan y won’t they jus give these guys a good ending 😭😭😭\n\nbridge fight was INSAAANEEE\n\nsuper cool how he has all those voices in his head to represent ravaanan’s pathu thala \n\nvikram’s performance was INNCREEEEDDIIIBBLEEE man if im being so honest i think the writing wasn’t like amazing but WOW the direction music cinematography everyone’s performances it all made up for it . he showed that feeling of like internal angst so so well \n\nsppoooilleeeerrssss !!!! \n\nending twist man that was so so so good . i love that when she goes back to vikram she’s dressed in full white (thanks niki) she’s in her purest form when she’s free of dev n then she’s stained red BECAUSE of dev returning loved that sm . idk the ramayana lore but i rly like how they humanised the antihero . it was so cool how when aish was telling veera the things dev said ab her he’s literally confused like he doesnt even understand why the so called “God-like man” has these thoughts of her yk . n the constraint n respect i guess to never touch or hit ragini compared to what dev thought veera was doing to her yeah man this is cinema \n\nnaan varuvene such a perfect song to end off the movie",
