    "review": "goat scene nearly made me cry in the cinema\n\ndidn’t miss sana too much (which i was NOT expecting to say icl i was so sad at first that both vetrimaaran and mari were making movies without sana, his style of music is literally MADEEE for their movies) , prasanna was v good too espec w the score . theekoluthi and kaalamaadan gaanam are BAAANGEERSSSS , it felt v similar to the pariyerum perumal soundtrack \n\nbeautiful beautiful cinematography\n\ndhruv was phenomenal , MEGA improvement from mahaan so proud of him . don’t even need to mention pasupathy bro when has he NOT BEEN GOATED !!!\n\nlowk didn’t need a love track ? crazy from me but it didn’t feel like it added that much emotionally to the story and u guys KNOW how much i love a good romance in movies\n\ni lowk went to the tsoc kabbadi event only cos i watched this movie lmao . gave me mega flashbacks to when i used to play back in eelam, i was an agile little kid man take me back to those days 💔 \n\nwent in completely entirely blind NO music NO trailer not even a poster or review n my GOD was it worth it 😭😭😭\n\nameer 😻😻😻 was getting MEGA vada chennai vibes bro he’s so cold i love him . in fact that whole gang war aspect i really enjoyed like don’t get me wrong i adoooreddd the kabbadi aspect it was so emotionally complex w the caste undertones and all but the gang stuff added a whoooleee extra layer of moral ambiguity to it yk i love that sm . \n\nbest tamil movie of 2025 for me",
