    "review": "CUTE KITTIES AWWWIIEEEEEE madam reminded me of vaanu so much\n\nTEEJAY !!!!!! WHAT THE FUUCKCKCKKK I LOVE SEEING HIM IN MOVIES but im ngl casting him and NOT putting him on the album is disgraceful work i mean have you HEARD muttu muttu ?!?!? \n\nanyway speaking of the album what a banger dude had proper nice chill almost jazz vibes , loved it so much \n\nvisually so beautiful too i liked all the dramatic contrasty lighting\n\nanyway ab the movie itself icl first of all vetrimaaran my goat for even producing this cos didnt the trailer get banned in india ??? that punda cbfc bro even tho i didn’t love the movie i HAVE to commend them for even writing this story yk \n\nlike u guys know how male indian audiences are n this time its not even the boomers bro its ppl our age hating on the movie which is like ??? 😭😭😭 n i saw sooooo many ppl saying oh imagine if the roles were reversed as if guys don’t glaze animal n all the other srv movies for having toxic protagonists wallahi piss off man 😭 i liked that they didn’t glorify ramya at all like she acc has to deal w the consequences of her decisions , in fact the movie lowk makes her life ROUGH bro like poor girl 😭 \n\nI LOOOVEEDDDD the mother daughter dynamic bro like that was SUPER well written . obvs as a guy i couldn’t relate to the story as much as most of my friends could but the mother daughter subplot was v good , espec that one scene where her mum was yelling at her but then the grandma starting yelling at her mum , n she turned to her husband expecting him to support her n he just doesn’t , n then ramya n her mum r in the same situation THATS GOOD WRITIIINNGGG\n\ni liked the message of that subplot yk cos yes ramya’s mum does jus want the best for her that’s why she struggles so much w teaching n tutoring n all to provide for her future but at the same time it feels like she’s prioritising that over her happiness which is where all that resentment came from in the same place like it’s just misplaced affection yk ? like i really want to be mad at her mum but at the same time it’s her first time being a mum , she just doesn’t want ramya to struggle the way she did n it jus reminds me of my own parents so much \n\ni also rly liked how it was a proper coming of age type of film but it didnt have the same like everything is solved life is great now ending yk? like in the end she gets the house that she dreamed ab at the start but she never got to build it with the man in her dreams n idk i thought it was kinda poetic yk",
