    "review": "dear vaanu\n\nhow lucky was i,\nto feel the pressure of your paws, kneading trust into my skin\nto feel the pulse of your heart when you drifted to sleep on my chest\nto have my laptop held hostage by your weight on its keys, a quiet protest against my work\nto have you wait patiently for treats whilst i’m already late to leave \nto see you run towards me every time i come home\nhow lucky to see you hide away every time someone new entered the house, only to become your sanctuary when you were afraid\nto have to clean up after you every time you used the litter box\nto be mad at you every time you threw up on the sofa\nto have all my clothes ruined by your thick fur\nto have to breathe through allergy pills and sneezes\njust to steal one more hour with you by my side\n\nhow lucky am i,\nto know what it’s like to love and be loved unconditionally \nto be reminded of you in all of my brightest moments, even as you haunt them\nto have my eyes turned fragile in your absence\nto feel my throat clench when i think of you again\nto have you spend your first and last day,\nengulfed in the warmth of my bed\nyou are a fleeting shadow now, a glimpse i catch in the corner of my eye\ni have returned you to the soil of the same garden you loved playing in\ntucked into the same clothes you made so beautiful with your fur\n\nand how lucky will i be,\nto one day show all the love i showed you to a new soul, \ncarrying lessons of love only you could teach\nto have you gaze over me as i grow older,\nlearning to grieve and to love through you \nto smile at another and feel your whiskers nudging my memory \nto etch your portrait into my skin, so i don’t have to look far to find you\nand to one day meet you again where you rest, walking through the final door to find you running to meet me again \n\ntwo years was never going to be enough, \nbut you were so small, and yet you left the biggest hole in my heart \n\nyou’re resting peacefully in eternity now\nbut you’re still here, \nembroidered in all the shirts i own,\nwoven in the very way i breathe",
