    "review": "beautiful movie man i cried like a stupid baby wasn’t expecting that at all\n\ni was smiling a lot throughout the first half , seeing this unconditional love they had for each other and the peace they found within each other , even in the quiet moments , felt so beautiful to me . i found myself yearning to have a best friend like that , someone who you can exist with and still feel that quiet love with , and i realised i had that with vaanu . at the end when fujino flashes through different moments she had with kyomoto hit me a lot , it’s the same feeling i get when i go thru my cam roll and see random moments i spent just existing with her . \n\nand again the part where she starts blaming herself for kyomoto’s death i felt my throat clenching, i found myself doing that a lot over this past week . trying to peek into these alternative timelines where i had just done the right thing , where i was just a better owner . but in the end the movie reminded me that these ‘what if’ scenarios are just the price of loving someone so much it leaves you fragile . it’s a beautiful yet painful reminder that even if the friendship is short , the shadow of their soul stays with you forever \n\nso grateful for the runtime , i’ve been struggling to focus on anything at all this past week and so this was the perfect length for me . at the same time i was so upset i didn’t get to spend more time with these two and be happy with them , but at the same time i guess that just plays on the idea of a life cut short unexpectedly and unfairly \n\nlove u forever vaanu",
